     "p": {
      "ar": "`element.style.setProperty(\"--progress\", \"65%\")` بيغيّر متغير، والـ CSS يكمّل الباقي (عرض، لون، حركة). ده أنضف من تعديل 5 خصائص من JS — والمنطق يفضل في CSS.",
      "en": "`element.style.setProperty(\"--progress\", \"65%\")` changes a variable and CSS does the rest (width, colour, motion). Cleaner than changing 5 properties from JS — and the logic stays in CSS."
     },
     "ex": "<style>\n  .bar { --progress: 0%; height: 14px; border-radius: 99px; background: #e5e9ee; overflow: hidden; max-width: 360px; font-family: system-ui; }\n  .bar::after { content: \"\"; display: block; height: 100%; width: var(--progress); background: #0a7d32; transition: width .4s ease; }\n</style>\n<p>Orders synced: <output id=\"pct\">0%</output></p>\n<div class=\"bar\" id=\"bar\"></div>\n<button id=\"step\">+ 15%</button>\n<script>\n  let p = 0;\n  document.getElementById(\"step\").onclick = () => {\n    p = Math.min(100, p + 15);\n    document.getElementById(\"bar\").style.setProperty(\"--progress\", p + \"%\");\n    document.getElementById(\"pct\").textContent = p + \"%\";\n  };\n</script>",
